-- Retired: index_usage_report(bigint) and index_usage_detail(text, integer).
--
-- entity_type_counts_approx / partition_pressure were retired here when they had
-- zero callers (g4_dead_canonical). They are live again on PR #919 (GH #813/#764)
-- and called from substrate_pulse — do NOT re-drop them.
--
-- WHY A DROP MODULE AND NOT JUST DELETING THE .sql.in FILES. Removing a file from the
-- manifests stops FUTURE installs from creating the function. It does nothing to a database
-- that already ran an upgrade carrying it — ALTER EXTENSION ... UPDATE has no mechanism to
-- retract a CREATE that a previous version performed. Those catalogs would keep the
-- instruments indefinitely, and the gate would never flag them again because the gate
-- scans SOURCE, not pg_proc.
--
-- IF EXISTS throughout: a fresh install never created these, and this module runs there too.
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS index_usage_report(bigint);
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS index_usage_detail(text, integer);
